    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0835" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews files, lot 53 D 413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commander in Chief
                        Far East (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-02-27T16:28:00-05:00">February 27, 1953—4:28
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>JCS 932476. From JCS reur CX 61323.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d409-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Authy granted you in JCS 931969<anchor n="2" xml:id="d409-f2"/> extended
                        to include authy bring to trial POWs charged with acts of violence against
                        other POWs, taking place subsequent to POW segregation and relocation. You
                        also authorized try POWs who foment or participate in riots or
                        demonstrations which take place subsequent to receipt this msg. Authy re
                        cases involving past riots or demonstrations continues to be
                        withheld.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>No objection ur proposal confer with ofcrs re nominations to comsn. State
                        advised govts concerned in order assist obtaining full cooperation.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In view of extension authy granted herein careful consideration shld be
                        given to order in which cases are brought trial. In order create more
                        favorable polit atmosphere it has been suggested trials rotate among cases
                        involving acts against UNC psnl, acts committed by Commies and acts
                        committed by anti-Commies against fellow POWs. However, order of trials left
                        to ur discretion.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
